Task: OrderStore.updateStatusByItemId returns order details (US-5.3, Phase 1)

Summary: Changed OrderStore.updateStatusByItemId's return type from F[Boolean]
to F[Option[UpdatedOrderRef]] so StockEventConsumer can build order.reserved's
payload (orderId/customerId/totalCents) without a second query. Added
UpdatedOrderRef case class. Extended the Postgres impl's RETURNING clause to
return id/customer_id/total_cents atomically instead of just id. Updated the
in-memory impl to match. StockEventConsumer's logOutcome helper now pattern-
matches Option instead of Boolean; its two call sites needed no changes since
they already passed the result through a `_` placeholder.

Files changed:
- src/main/scala/orderservice/OrderStore.scala (UpdatedOrderRef, trait,
  in-memory impl, Postgres query + impl)
- src/main/scala/orderservice/StockEventConsumer.scala (logOutcome)
- src/test/scala/orderservice/OrderStoreSuite.scala (updated 3 tests)
- src/test/scala/orderservice/OrderStorePostgresSuite.scala (updated 4 tests)
- src/test/scala/orderservice/HealthRoutesSuite.scala (2 stub signatures)
- src/test/scala/orderservice/OrderRoutesSuite.scala (2 stub signatures)
- conductor/tracks.md (marked track in progress)

Why: US-5.3 needs to publish order.reserved once an order is Reserved, but
the consumer only had a Boolean and an orderItemId - not enough to build the
payload. Fetching the needed fields in the same atomic UPDATE...RETURNING
avoids a second round-trip and a race window.
